   "text": "Day 2/30 \u2014 Gavin Uberti\n\nFor Day 2, I redesigned the LinkedIn profile of Gavin Uberti, CEO and Co-Founder of Etched.\n\nHis profile is interesting because the credibility is already there.\n\nCEO amp; Co-Founder @ Etched.\n\nHarvard.\n\n14K+ followers.\n\nA company building hardware for superintelligence.\nA strong track record across AI and engineering.\n\nAnd his content makes it clear that he\u2019s deeply involved in what he\u2019s building.\n\nBut that raised a different question for me:\n\nDoes his profile communicate all of that quickly enough?\n\nHis original headline is simply:\n\nCEO and Co-Founder @ Etched\n\nIt\u2019s clean.\n\nBut it leaves a lot of context on the table.\n\nSomeone landing on his profile should quickly ",
